# This repo is PUBLIC (GitHub Pages), but most of what's in this folder is
# personal health data. Deny by default and allow only what's meant to be
# published, so an accidental `git add -A` can't leak measurements.
#
# Ignored on purpose: RENPHO *.csv (raw measurements), reports/ (report PDFs),
# segmental_data.jsonl (extracted values), _work/ (logs + CSV backups).
*

# The published dashboard — data is embedded in it deliberately.
!dashboard.html
!.gitignore

# The ingest pipeline itself. Published so the daemon machines can pull code
# updates (`_sync_from_origin` fast-forwards before each build) instead of
# needing the scripts copied over by hand. No credentials live in these — the
# publish identity is a noreply address and git auth comes from the machine.
!process_pdfs.py
!pdfimg.py
!ocr_segmental.py

# To publish something else (e.g. the README) un-ignore it here explicitly, e.g.:
#   !README.md
